- validate format/version before creating anything;
- remap every UUID and polymorphic/foreign-key reference;
- rebind users by exported email, make the importing identity owner, and preserve other people;
- regenerate secrets, publication keys, blob keys, and instance-specific SGIDs;
- stream each file directly into the configured Active Storage service;
- wrap all database changes in one transaction and delete any physical objects if anything fails.

I’ll expose the importer independently of the web lifecycle first and prove export→import round trips atomically.

